@@section 1
@@title SQ-EX Exposure Extras camera bag ids through Common's swap list, 2026-11-17 ([exposure.md](../exposure.md) 8, design_rules V-06; TODO `conventions #23`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-17
@@jars exposure creativecommon
@@sources development/exposureBackport/src/extras
@@text
@@text The hand `MissingMappingsEvent` in `ExposureExtras` is gone: `creativeengineering:<tier>_camera_bag` (before patcherMod 1.0.3) and `exposure_extras:*` are `replaces` entries in `data/exposureextras/swaps/owner_namespace.json`. Runs in boot 2 of SQ-RFX-25 (rows/RFX.qb section 6); the NBT alias half is SQ-RFX-27.
@@table
## SQ-EX-01 | camera bags load under exposureextras ids; no hand remap left
@group A (old save, boot 2 of SQ-RFX-25)
@commands `grep -E "\[swaps\]" logs/latest.log`; `> setblock 30 -61 0 chest{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"creativeengineering:iron_camera_bag",Count:1b,tag:{CameraBag:{}}}]}`; `> data get block 30 -61 0 Items`; `> give @p exposureextras:leather_camera_bag`
@pass the chest holds `exposureextras:iron_camera_bag` with its `CameraBag` tag; the give works; boot log has the `[swaps] ... list file(s)` line counting the Exposure Extras list and no `[exposureextras]` remap line; no missing-registry warning for any `camera_bag`
@fails the bag gone: the `creativeengineering:` entries are missing from Exposure's swap list (Creative Common reads `data/exposureextras/swaps/`)
> setblock 30 -61 0 chest{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"creativeengineering:iron_camera_bag",Count:1b,tag:{CameraBag:{}}}]}
> data get block 30 -61 0 Items
expect exposureextras:iron_camera_bag
shell ! grep -E "[Mm]issing.*camera_bag|Identifier .*camera_bag.* is missing" logs/latest.log
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command)
